IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja1-part1-preliminary.l4: Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 July 2024. LAYER 1, Part 1 (ss 1-2). The source is a plain-text rendering, not the official text.
-- Every name begins with the section it implements. Imports the keel's `scja-core` only.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the Act does not answer
-- on these facts and is never to be read as FALSE (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- s 1 (short title) is machinery and has no rule here.

§ `Part 1: Preliminary`

§§ `Section 2: Interpretation`

-- "unless the context otherwise requires": the gate on every definition below. The Act does not say what a word means when the context
-- does require otherwise, so the gate answers only whether this section's definitions govern (fork F1, NOTES.md; question QA).
-- src:378 | 2. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 2 (opening words) (src:378)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision you are reading require a different meaning?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the definitions of this section govern the word here` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Plain gloss: is this court the Appellate Division of the High Court?
-- src:379 | “Appellate Division” means the Appellate Division of the High
-- src:380 | Court;
@ref s 2 “Appellate Division” (src:379-380)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Appellate Division: the court is the Appellate Division of the High Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means"

-- Plain gloss: is this the court the Act calls "court" (GD, AD or CA)? The Singapore International Commercial Court is a division of the
-- General Division (s 18A); the definition does not name it (fork K1 of the keel).
-- src:381 | “court” means the General Division, the Appellate Division, or
-- src:382 | the Court of Appeal;
@ref s 2 “court” (src:381-382)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 court: the court is the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): s 18A makes it a division of the General Division, s 2 does not name it
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means"

-- Plain gloss: is this the Family Division of the High Court (the Family Justice Act 2014 constitutes it; that Act is not among the sources)?
-- src:383 | “Family Division of the High Court” means the Family Division
-- src:384 | of the High Court constituted under section 4 of the Family
-- src:385 | Justice Act 2014;
@ref s 2 “Family Division of the High Court” (src:383-385)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Family Division of the High Court: the court is the Family Division of the High Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Family Division of the High Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means"

-- Plain gloss: are these the Family Justice Rules? Both limbs are facts about the rules, borrowed from the Family Justice Act 2014.
-- src:392 | “Family Justice Rules” means the Family Justice Rules made
-- src:393 | under the Family Justice Act 2014 and any other written law
-- src:394 | by the Family Justice Rules Committee constituted under
-- src:395 | section 46(1) of that Act;
@ref s 2 “Family Justice Rules” (src:392-395)
GIVEN `they were made under the Family Justice Act 2014 or any other written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the rules made under the Family Justice Act 2014 or any other written law?
      `they were made by the Family Justice Rules Committee constituted under section 46(1) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the rules made by the Family Justice Rules Committee constituted under section 46(1) of the Family Justice Act 2014?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Family Justice Rules: the instrument is the Family Justice Rules` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `they were made under the Family Justice Act 2014 or any other written law`
           AND `they were made by the Family Justice Rules Committee constituted under section 46(1) of that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means"

-- Plain gloss: is this the General Division of the High Court? (K1: the Singapore International Commercial Court is a division of it.)
-- src:397 | “General Division” means the General Division of the High
-- src:398 | Court;
@ref s 2 “General Division” (src:397-398)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 General Division: the court is the General Division of the High Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): s 18A makes it "a division of the General Division"; s 2 does not say whether "General Division" includes it
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means"

-- Plain gloss: is this person a Judge for the purposes of the Act? (the opening words of the definition; limbs (a) to (c) follow)
-- src:400 | “Judge” means a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial
-- src:401 | Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge,
-- src:402 | and —
@ref s 2 “Judge” (src:400-402)
GIVEN j IS A Judge
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` j EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF j's office EQUALS `Judicial Commissioner` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF j's office EQUALS `Senior Judge` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF j's office EQUALS `International Judge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means"

-- s 2 "Judge" (a): in relation to the General Division, a Judge sitting in that Division in accordance with the Constitution and this Act.
-- The Constitution is not among the sources: whether the sitting is "in accordance with" it is a fact asked of the person.
-- src:404 | (a) in relation to the General Division, means a Judge
-- src:405 | sitting in that Division in accordance with the
-- src:406 | Constitution and this Act;
@ref s 2 “Judge” (a) (src:404-406)
GIVEN j IS A Judge
      `sits in the General Division in accordance with the Constitution and this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Judge sitting in the General Division in accordance with the Constitution and the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Judge (a): in relation to the General Division, the person is a Judge sitting in that Division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` j EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `sits in the General Division in accordance with the Constitution and this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a Judge sitting in that Division in accordance with the Constitution and this Act"

-- s 2 "Judge" (b): the same for the Appellate Division.
-- src:408 | (b) in relation to the Appellate Division, means a Judge
-- src:409 | sitting in that Division in accordance with the
-- src:410 | Constitution and this Act; and
@ref s 2 “Judge” (b) (src:408-410)
GIVEN j IS A Judge
      `sits in the Appellate Division in accordance with the Constitution and this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Judge sitting in the Appellate Division in accordance with the Constitution and the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Judge (b): in relation to the Appellate Division, the person is a Judge sitting in that Division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` j EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `sits in the Appellate Division in accordance with the Constitution and this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a Judge sitting in that Division in accordance with the Constitution and this Act"

-- s 2 "Judge" (c): the same for the Court of Appeal ("that Court").
-- src:412 | (c) in relation to the Court of Appeal, means a Judge
-- src:413 | sitting in that Court in accordance with the
-- src:414 | Constitution and this Act;
@ref s 2 “Judge” (c) (src:412-414)
GIVEN j IS A Judge
      `sits in the Court of Appeal in accordance with the Constitution and this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Judge sitting in the Court of Appeal in accordance with the Constitution and the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Judge (c): in relation to the Court of Appeal, the person is a Judge sitting in that Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` j EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `sits in the Court of Appeal in accordance with the Constitution and this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a Judge sitting in that Court in accordance with the Constitution and this Act"

-- Plain gloss: is this officer the Registrar as the Act uses the word? "means ... and includes": the Registrar and the Deputy and Assistant Registrars are named;
-- the "includes" leaves open whether anyone else counts, so any other officer is NOTHING (fork F3; marginal reading M1).
-- src:416 | “Registrar” means the Registrar of the Supreme Court and
-- src:417 | includes the Deputy Registrar and the Assistant Registrars;
@ref s 2 “Registrar” (src:416-417)
GIVEN officer IS AN `Officer of the Supreme Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Registrar: the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN Registrar THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Assistant Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means the Registrar of the Supreme Court and includes the Deputy Registrar and the Assistant Registrars"

-- Plain gloss: are these Rules of Court? Made under this Act: yes. A form: yes ("includes forms"). Anything else: the "includes" leaves it open (F3; M1).
-- src:419 | “Rules of Court” means Rules of Court made under this Act and
-- src:420 | includes forms;
@ref s 2 “Rules of Court” (src:419-420)
GIVEN `they are rules made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they rules of court made under the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969?
      `it is a form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Rules of Court: the instrument is Rules of Court made under this Act or a form` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `they are rules made under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a form` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means Rules of Court made under this Act and includes forms"

-- Plain gloss: is this a seal as the Act uses the word? A stamp counts; the "includes" does not close the list.
-- src:422 | “seal” includes stamp;
@ref s 2 “seal” (src:422)
GIVEN `it is a seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a seal?
      `it is a stamp` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a stamp?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 seal: the thing is a seal or a stamp` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a seal` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a stamp` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“seal” includes stamp"

-- Plain gloss: is this a subordinate court? Courts under the State Courts Act 1970 (the District Court and Magistrate's Court of the core), a Family Court or Youth Court
-- under the Family Justice Act 2014, and any other court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body from whose decisions a written law gives a right of appeal to the Supreme Court.
-- A division of the Supreme Court itself: the Act does not say whether the "Supreme Court" in the last limb includes it (fork F4), so NOTHING.
-- src:424 | “subordinate court” means a court constituted under the State
-- src:425 | Courts Act 1970, a Family Court or Youth Court constituted
-- src:426 | under the Family Justice Act 2014, and any other court,
-- src:427 | tribunal or judicial or quasi‑judicial body from the decisions
-- src:428 | of which under any written law there is a right of appeal to the
-- src:429 | Supreme Court;
@ref s 2 “subordinate court” (src:424-429)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law give a right of appeal from this body's decisions to the Supreme Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `District Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Family Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Youth Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Syariah Court` THEN
        IF `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" ... "any other court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body from the decisions of which under any written law there is a right of appeal to the Supreme Court"
    WHEN `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` THEN
        IF `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" ... "any other court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body from the decisions of which under any written law there is a right of appeal to the Supreme Court"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "Supreme Court" is not defined in s 2 and the Act does not say whether a division of it is a subordinate court

-- Plain gloss: is this person one of the Judges the Act speaks of in "Supreme Court Judge" (see below)?
-- The Vice-President of the Court of Appeal is read as a Justice of the Court of Appeal, and the President of the Appellate Division as a Judge of the Appellate Division,
-- because s 4(c) and 4(e) rank "the Justices of the Court of Appeal (other than the Vice-Presidents" and "the Judges of the Appellate Division (other than the President" (fork F2).
-- src:431 | “Supreme Court Judge” means the Chief Justice, a Justice of the
-- src:432 | Court of Appeal, a Judge of the Appellate Division or a Judge
-- src:433 | of the High Court.
@ref s 2 “Supreme Court Judge” (src:431-433)
GIVEN j IS A Judge
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` MEANS
    CONSIDER j's office
    WHEN `Chief Justice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Vice-President of the Court of Appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Justice of the Court of Appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `President of the Appellate Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Judge of the Appellate Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Judge of the High Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means"

-- s 1 (short title) and the opening words of s 2 aside, the definitions the Act scatters through later sections are encoded where they sit (ss 8(7), 17(2), 17A(9), 18D(3)).
